How the system works:
Ground Control Server (gc_server.py)
 - Provides the map, commands, and mine serial numbers via gRPC
 - Filters out digging commands ('D') as rovers no longer perform digging
 - Subscribes to the Defused-Mines channel to log disarmed mines

Rovers (rover_client.py)
 - Connect to Ground Control via gRPC
 - Retrieve map and commands from the Ground Control
 - Execute movement commands 
 - Does not dig anymore, so does not blow up anymore
 - Instead, it publishes demine tasks to RabbitMQ when they find mines

Deminers (deminers.py)
 - Subscribe to the Demine-Queue channel
 - Process one demine task at a time (if not busy)
 - Calculate the mine PIN through brute-force hashing
 - Publish the result to the Defused-Mines channel

For me:
source .venv/bin/activate
then cd to lab3

To check RabbitMQ:
sudo systemctl status rabbitmq-server
sudo systemctl enable rabbitmq-server
sudo systemctl start rabbitmq-server
127.0.0.1:15672 (guest, guest)

How to run:
Run the ground control server first.
python3 gc_server.py

Then run the deminers.
python3 deminer.py 1
python3 deminer.py 2

Then run the different rovers
python3 rover_client.py 1
python3 rover_client.py 2
python3 rover_client.py 3
...
python3 rover_client.py 10